      "poet_id": "53",
      "poet_name": "ربيعة بن مقروم",
      "note": "No reliable source found for death year; sources describe him as a mukhadram warrior-poet (fought at al-Qadisiyyah) but give no date of death."
    },
    {
      "poet_id": "1249",
      "poet_name": "ابن قيس الرُّقيّات",
      "note": "No reliable source found for an actual death year; a library authority record lists him as 'active 657-704' (an activity span, not a death date), and no biographical source found gives a specific death year."
    },
    {
      "poet_id": "1263",
      "poet_name": "مُليح بن الحكم",
      "note": "No reliable source found. Note: do not confuse with the hadith transmitter 'Abu al-Malih al-Hudhali' (d. 101-112 AH), a different person despite the similar name, who turned up repeatedly in searches for this poet."
    },
    {
      "poet_id": "1307",
      "poet_name": "المُرقِّشُ الأَصغر",
      "note": "No reliable source found for a death year. Pre-Islamic; described as nephew of al-Muraqqish al-Akbar and paternal uncle of Tarafa ibn al-'Abd, which places him in roughly the same mid-6th-century CE generation, but no specific year is documented in available sources."
    },
    {
      "poet_id": "1505",
      "poet_name": "السموأل بن عادياء",
      "note": "No reliable source found for a death year; sources (Jawad Ali's al-Mufassal, al-Zirikli's al-A'lam per citation only) describe his legendary 'loyalty' story (refusing to surrender Imru' al-Qais's armor) but none in this search gave a date of death, and some researchers question the story's historicity altogether."
    },
    {
      "poet_id": "1150",
      "poet_name": "تأبّطَ شَرًّا",
      "note": "No reliable source found for a specific death year. Wikipedia gives only an era ('late 6th or early 7th century CE'); an old English translation on Wikisource offers two speculative readings (shortly before 569 CE, the year of Muhammad's birth, or sometime in the 40 years between 569 and 609 CE), neither treated as established."
    },
    {
      "poet_id": "1566",
      "poet_name": "النجاشي الحارثي",
      "note": "No reliable source found for death year; described as a mukhadram satirist from Najran who settled in Kufa and was threatened by both 'Umar ibn al-Khattab and 'Ali, but no source found gives a date of death."
    },
    {
      "poet_id": "1570",
      "poet_name": "يزيد بن مفرغ الحميري",
      "note": "No reliable source found for death year; sources describe his conflict with and satire of 'Abbad ibn Ziyad under Umayyad governor 'Ubayd Allah ibn Ziyad, but none found gives a date of death."
    },
    {
      "poet_id": "1572",
      "poet_name": "أيمن بن خريم",
      "note": "No reliable source found for death year; biographical dictionaries found describe his lineage and a poem of reproach to Mu'awiya but give no date of death."
    },
    {
      "poet_id": "1400",
      "poet_name": "الحمدوي",
      "note": "No reliable source found for a specific death year. One source describes him as named after his grandfather Hamduwayh, who carried out the execution of heretics (zandaqa) under Harun al-Rashid (r. 786-809 CE), placing the poet in the early-to-mid Abbasid period, but no death year is given."
    },
    {
      "poet_id": "1676",
      "poet_name": "مجهول (شعراء عباسيون منسيون)",
      "note": "Anonymous/collective attribution ('unknown -- forgotten Abbasid poets'), not an individual -- no individual death year applicable."
    },
    {
      "poet_id": "1693",
      "poet_name": "عبيد بن الأخطل",
      "note": "No reliable source found. Search results only ever returned information about the major Umayyad poet al-Akhtal (Ghiyath ibn Ghawth al-Taghlibi, d. ~90-92 AH) or about the unrelated pre-Islamic poet 'Ubayd ibn al-Abras -- neither is confirmed as the same person as this corpus entry, and no source describing an 'Ubayd ibn al-Akhtal' was found."
    },
    {
      "poet_id": "1661",
      "poet_name": "عبد الله بن عبد الحميد اللاحقي",
      "note": "No reliable source found. Likely related to the attested poet Aban ibn 'Abd al-Hamid al-Lahiqi (same nisba/patronymic pattern), but no source found confirms the relationship or gives any biographical/death information for this specific name."
    },
    {
      "poet_id": "1306",
      "poet_name": "المُرَقِّشُ الأكبر (عمرو بن سعد بن مالك)",
      "note": "No reliable source found for a death year. One source mentions he worked as a scribe for al-Harith ibn Abi Shamir al-Ghassani 'around 524 CE' (a career anecdote, not a death date, and sourced from only one site); he died before his nephew al-Muraqqish al-Asghar."
    },
    {
      "poet_id": "1722",
      "poet_name": "القرآن الكريم",
      "note": "Not an individual poet -- Qur'anic text; no death year applicable."
    },
    {
